{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. Every testable obligation in the text maps to at least one test with assertions that enforce it. I judged this from the supplied test source alone and requested no implementation source.\n\n**Combining contributions and including every applicable one**\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` builds a subject with a cited requirement, a distant cited requirement, terms, an example, and `{impl}`/`{test}` references. It asserts that:\n  - the declaration, the cited base requirement, the example and the test node are included;\n  - the `{impl}` node, the whole `impl[Thing]` and the distant requirement are excluded;\n  - two definitions appear.\n- `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs` checks which edges contribute, in both directions, for a requirement, a cited example and a parent requirement.\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs`, `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` and `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes` cover anchors, outline-node selection, plain-text files, markdown sections, and acknowledgments (`{fixme}` references).\n- `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` covers the git-tracked case.\n- `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` and `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` check the mandatory set for citation and site reviews.\n\n**Deduplicating identical selections**\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` names the same file in both `:impl:` and `:test:`. It asserts an exact two-element list, so the file appears once.\n- The bundle test has mutually referencing terms and asserts exactly two definitions.\n- `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` repeats citations, a shared term and a built-in. It asserts each appears once and the total is 5.\n\n**Reporting unresolvable inputs before inference**\n- `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation`, `unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference` (a missing file, a missing node, and a disallowed path) and `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` check that preparation fails with the path in the error.\n- The staging test checks the `git add` hint for untracked declarations and terms.\n- The CLI test `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` asserts a nonzero exit, the path on stderr, no connection to the model endpoint, and unchanged evidence.\n- `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` checks that stale recorded inputs are not mandatory.\n\n**Complete set in the initial model request**\n- The citation and site tests check that the initial prompt contains the mandatory inputs. The site test compares the subject message exactly with the filled template built from `model_mandatory_inputs`.\n- `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` checks that the prompt contains the selected node and not its sibling.\n- The CLI tests `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` and `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` check the prompt over real requests. They find the requirement, the definition and the test node in it, and `{impl}` text absent.\n- `model_inputs_reads_searches_and_citation_prompts_are_redacted` checks redaction of the mandatory inputs and prompt.\n\n**Generated `evidence/` output**\n- `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` covers every case in the text:\n  - the default exclusion omits an `evidence/` anchor without aborting;\n  - a symlink alias into `evidence/` is omitted too (unix only);\n  - an explicit allow includes the file;\n  - an explicit disallow aborts with `PermissionDenied` and the path in the error.\n- `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` and `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` check that earlier evidence, and references discovered inside it, do not leak into the inputs.\n\n**Delegated or out of scope**\n- The batch and exit-status behaviour belongs to `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`, which is cited here and needs no test of its own here.\n- The obligation that contributing requirements cite this requirement and define their contributions is a documentation convention. It is not behaviour a test can check, and the contributing requirements carry it.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behaviour that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "de1a2b1d19c29af774a8993d3d101cba2888ecfa96eb1fb8508aa56af15f665d",
